{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790015023,"nonce":"l8feQclcCRSeChtJOFuMZaHCX6s=","title":"On-screen messages (Messages.Message) never reach the journal or digest","message":"Found while testing Prison Standards on the bench, 2026-09-21.\n\n## The gap\n`Messages.Message`, the top-left text messages, never reaches the journal or `digest`. Vanilla and mods report a lot through it:\n- \"X refused to be arrested\";\n- `MessageNoWardenOfIdeo`;\n- Prison Standards' \"Skippy finished the prison plan and stays on maintain only.\" and \"skipped Convert: …\".\n\n`dev:debug-action` (7b8d573) captures messages only during its own call.\n\nTo verify Prison Standards' messages I had to `save` and grep `\u003ctext\u003e` in the .rws archive. A message sent with `historical: false` would not even be there.\n\n## Ask\nJournal each `Messages.Message` as an event carrying:\n- the text;\n- the MessageTypeDef;\n- the lookTargets (thing ids and cells);\n- the tick.\n\nOptionally, `digest` shows the ones since the last look.\n\n## Acceptance\n- A message raised during an `advance` appears in `journal --verb` with its text, type and target ids, whether or not it's historical.\n- A message raised while paused (e.g. from a verb) appears too.","files":null}]}